# Six of the ten delimiters, each with its own terminal.
#
# The C's table is ten rows crossed with interpolation, and the row is chosen
# by which terminal the parse state admits rather than by the bytes - so a
# book gets the closing byte right for `)` and wrong for `>` without any
# single file noticing. All six in one file is the cheapest way to make one
# wrong row visible.
roots 1
mends 0
holds quoted_content
spans quoted_content 7 11
spans quoted_content 24 28
spans quoted_content 41 47
spans quoted_content 60 65
spans quoted_content 78 83
spans quoted_content 96 100
